course: dictionary
lesson: 5773
title: Words from the sky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from smaller parts, and the parts give you clues. Lunisolar is built from «lun», which comes from the Latin word for Moon, and «solar», which means of the Sun. Put them together and you get based on both the Moon and the Sun.
explain: The sentence gives you a clue too: «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year because they follow lunar or lunisolar calendars.» The brackets explain it: calendars that follow the Moon, or the Moon and the Sun together. Lunisolar is one of those two kinds.
explain: A lunisolar calendar makes its months by following the Moon. Because the Moon's cycle is shorter than the Sun's year, the calendar now and then adds an extra month. This keeps it in step with the seasons and the Sun.
fact: Lunisolar means based on both the Moon and the Sun.
fact: A lunisolar calendar makes months from the Moon and keeps the year in step with the Sun.
fact: The Chinese, Hebrew and Hindu calendars are lunisolar.
fact: «Lunar» means of the Moon, and «solar» means of the Sun.
fact: Because lunisolar calendars follow the Moon, festivals like Chinese New Year and Passover fall on different dates each year.
exercise: «Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah and Lunar New Year fall on different dates each year.» Why do their dates change? | Because the weather changes | *Because they follow calendars based on the Moon, or the Moon and the Sun | Because they are always on 25 December | Because the Sun moves to a new place each year
exercise: What does lunisolar mean? | *Based on both the Moon and the Sun | Based on the seasons only | Based on the stars and the rain | Based on the Sun only
exercise: Lunisolar is built from two word parts. Which part means the Moon? | *Lun | Nis | Ar | Sol
test: In a lunisolar calendar, what does the extra month do? | Makes the Sun rise later | Stops the Moon from shining | *Keeps the calendar in step with the seasons and the Sun | Makes the year longer for no reason
test: Chinese New Year changes its date each year. What kind of calendar does it come from? | *A lunisolar calendar | A digital calendar on a phone | A solar calendar with the same date every year | A calendar with no months at all
exam: «Passover falls on a different date each year.» Which best explains why? | Passover is always on the same day of the Sun's year | *Its calendar is lunisolar, so it follows the Moon and adds months to stay in step with the seasons | Passover is moved by the weather | Passover depends on the number of people who celebrate it
